<Ui>
    <!--
        benilla's Skills tab (decision 0437 phase 4): the 1.12 `SkillFrame`, re-expressed from the
        reference FrameXML `SkillFrame.{xml,lua}` (session scratchpad `ref-ui/`, decision 0246
        discipline — never committed) onto our own engine/feeds. Geometry/art-paths below are QUOTED
        from the ref (line citations inline, into that same `SkillFrame.xml`/`.lua`); the Lua is
        the ref's logic turned onto benilla's Era API (`GetNumSkillLines`/`GetSkillLineInfo`/
        `Expand`/`CollapseSkillHeader`/`SetSelectedSkill`/`GetSelectedSkill`, decision 0437's skills
        seam, `crates/benilla-ui/src/script/skills.rs`, built alongside this file).

        A CHILD PAGE of `CharacterFrame` (ref: `parent="CharacterFrame"`, `id="4"` — ours too, since
        the Reputation page landed and took slot 3 back), shown/
        hidden by `CharacterFrame_ShowSubFrame` exactly like `PaperDollFrame` — but NOT a
        physically nested `<Frame>` the way PaperDollFrame is: PaperDollFrame is declared INSIDE
        CharacterFrame.xml's own `<Frames>` tree (a real engine parent/child), while this page is a
        SEPARATE file's top-level `<Frame>` (CharacterFrame.xml is shared-tree with another session
        this pass, so only its tab machinery is touched here — not its frame tree). `parent=` is
        transcribed for fidelity but is a NO-OP in this engine (grepped `benilla-ui/src/loader`: the
        XML `parent` attribute is read nowhere — only physical `<Frames>` nesting creates a real
        parent). Position instead rides `<Anchors relativeTo="CharacterFrame">` (a NAMED
        lookup, works regardless of tree position, the same mechanism every sibling-anchor in this
        codebase already uses) — loaded right after `CharacterFrame.xml` in the load list so it
        paints ON TOP of it (later file = higher z, the established house convention every top-level
        window already relies on implicitly). Because a true engine Hide-cascade doesn't reach a
        non-child, `CharacterFrame.xml`'s own `CharacterFrame_OnHide` was extended (its own
        header comment) to loop-hide every `BENILLA_CHARACTERFRAME_SUBFRAMES` entry — the fix this
        page's non-nested shape requires, done once so later non-nested tabs (Pet/Reputation/Honor)
        inherit it for free.

        NO OWN PORTRAIT (matches the ref: `ref-ui/SkillFrame.xml` l.130-213 draws no portrait Texture
        at all): the shared quadrant background art below (`UI-Character-General-TopLeft/TopRight`,
        the SAME "General" variant the ref uses, l.136-159) carries the SAME baked-in portrait-ring
        cutout every PaperDollInfoFrame quadrant variant shares, so `CharacterFrame`'s own
        portrait/name/level (drawn at a lower z, underneath) shows through unchanged — exactly the
        ref's own real-client compositing (SkillFrame is a nested child there too, relying on the
        same cutout rather than redrawing the portrait itself).

        FLAT layout (TrainerFrame.xml/TradeSkillFrame.xml's own house constraint): this window has no
        DETAIL FontStrings needing a nested child Frame in the first place — the minimal detail pane
        (below) is a single StatusBar instance whose own name/rank FontStrings live on ITS OWN Layers
        (a StatusBar, like a Button, renders its own Layers fine — only a plain child `<Frame>` loses
        them), the exact `BenillaTradeSkillRankFrame` shape TradeSkillFrame.xml already proved.

        v1 DEVIATIONS (each re-cited at its own site below):
          1. THE DETAIL PANE IS MINIMAL-PLUS-DESCRIPTION-PLUS-ABANDON: the selected skill's rank
             StatusBar + name + the DESCRIPTION BODY (`SkillDetailDescriptionText` — ref
             `SkillDetailDescriptionText`/`SKILL_DESCRIPTION`, real since `GetSkillLineInfo`'s 13th
             return carries `SkillLine.dbc` col 12) + the ABANDON BUTTON
             (`SkillDetailUnlearnButton` → the `UNLEARN_SKILL` confirm → `AbandonSkill` →
             `CMSG_UNLEARN_SKILL`; the isAbandonable predicate is `SkillRaceClassInfo.flags & 0x20`
             — the server's own gate, real 5875 data: primary professions only). STILL OMITTED:
             the training-point spend row (the ref's `LeftArrow`/`RightArrow`/`LearnSkillButton`/
             `SkillDetailCostText`, all driven by `stepCost`/`rankCost`, which `GetSkillLineInfo`
             always reports nil/0 — 0437's own named out-of-scope: 1.12 training points are dead
             data).
          2. NO SORT CHECKBOX (ref l.215-241's own XML-commented-out "Replace once code is ready..."
             `SkillSortButton`): the ref itself ships this dead/commented, so there is nothing to
             transcribe (TradeSkillFrame.xml's own "ref's own dead code is dropped" precedent).
          3. NO ACCEPT/CANCEL BUTTONS (ref l.318-357's `SkillFrameAcceptButton`/`SkillFrameCancelButton`,
             the latter ALSO commented dead in the ref): both back the training-point economy (Accept/
             CancelSkillUps) this pane doesn't ship, AND this page has no window of its own to close —
             `CharacterFrame`'s single shared close X (CharacterFrame.xml) already covers every
             tab, matching `PaperDollFrame`'s own lack of a per-page close button.
          4. THE RANK TEXT FORMAT IS THE REF'S BYTE-EXACT ONE, not the task brief's own paraphrase:
             `ref-ui/SkillFrame.lua` l.178-186 builds `rank .. " (" .. color .. modifier .. close ..
             ")/" .. max` (e.g. "57 (|cff20ff20+3|r)/75") — transcribed verbatim (the
             reference file is the authority on the tuple/format, the brief's prose is a summary).
          5. NO FILLBAR (ref's `$parentFillBar`, driven by `numTempPoints`): [`GetSkillLineInfo`]
             always reports `numTempPoints = 0` (skills.rs's own module doc — 1.12 training points are
             dead data), so the fill bar could never show — dropped outright, `TradeSkillFrame.xml`'s
             OWN `BenillaTradeSkillRankFrame` (the identical StatusBar shape) already sets this local
             precedent for the same reason.
          6. NO HOVER TOOLTIP on a row: the ref's own `SkillFrame.lua` calls `GameTooltip` NOWHERE
             (grepped the full reference file) — a skill line is pure descriptor state, nothing to
             preview. Unlike Trainer/TradeSkill, this window needs no `GameTooltip:Set*Item` channel.
          7. `LockHighlight`/`UnlockHighlight` ENGINE GAP (TalentFrame.xml/TradeSkillFrame.xml's own
             "no engine equivalent" posture, grepped `benilla-ui/src/script/button.rs` — ships
             texture-pairs/SetText/Enable/Disable/RegisterForClicks/SetButtonState/Click only): the
             persistent selection glow is `SkillHighlight`, the separate overlay Frame
             Trainer/TradeSkillFrame already use, moved onto the selected row's StatusBar.
          8. GlobalStrings this window itself needs: NONE beyond the tab label `SKILLS` (already
             declared in CharacterFrame.xml, quoted there byte-exact with its GlobalStrings.lua line
             cite) — the ref's own `SkillFrame.lua` reads no other GlobalString.

        Rows repaint on `SKILL_LINES_CHANGED` (registered here; `crates/benilla/src/ui_char.rs`'s
        `watch_skill_ups`/`feed_skills` already fire it) and on `OnShow` (ref `SkillFrame_OnShow`,
        l.4-6). The list is the house faux-scroll kit (ScrollTemplates.xml, the TrainerFrame/
        TradeSkillFrame precedent) over 12 fixed row slots (ref `SKILLS_TO_DISPLAY = 12`,
        `SkillFrame.lua:1` — the ref's own row count, and this page shares the ref's own 384×512
        coordinate space since it fills the identical CharacterFrame page area).
    -->
    <Script><![CDATA[
        -- ── Constants (ref SkillFrame.lua:1-2) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        local SKILLFRAME_SKILLS_DISPLAYED = 12 -- SKILLS_TO_DISPLAY
        local SKILLFRAME_SKILL_HEIGHT = 15     -- SKILLFRAME_SKILL_HEIGHT

        -- GlobalStrings (ref GlobalStrings.lua:3478), chunk-local per the codebase idiom — safe
        -- because only THIS chunk's functions read it; the nil-"All" trap (TradeSkillFrame.xml's
        -- deviation notes) is the inline-XML-handler case, and no inline handler references it.
        -- Its earlier ABSENCE here made format() throw in UpdateDetail on every row selection —
        -- half of the 2026-07-17 "tabs are flaky" report (the silent-error half).
        local SKILL_DESCRIPTION = "|cffffffff%s|r %s"
        local UNLEARN_SKILL = "Do you want to unlearn %s?"      -- GlobalStrings.lua:4446
        local UNLEARN = "Unlearn"                               -- GlobalStrings.lua:4445
        local UNLEARN_SKILL_TOOLTIP = "Unlearn this profession" -- GlobalStrings.lua:4447

        -- Paint the rank StatusBar `bar` + its `SkillName`/`SkillRank` FontStrings for one skill-line
        -- ENTRY row (never a header — callers guard that): the ref's own bar-fill + rank-text half of
        -- `SkillFrame_SetStatusBar` (l.76-187) and the detail's twin `SkillDetailFrame_SetStatusBar`
        -- (l.161-187, l.370-399) — the SAME formatting either pane uses, factored once here since our
        -- minimal detail pane (deviation 1) needs nothing else from that function.
        function BenillaSkillFrame_PaintBar(bar, skillName, skillRank, skillModifier, skillMaxRank)
            local nameText = getglobal(bar:GetName() .. "SkillName")
            local rankText = getglobal(bar:GetName() .. "SkillRank")
            -- The trough behind the fill (ref `$parentBackground`), recoloured per branch alongside
            -- the fill itself — ref SkillFrame.lua:158 (normal) and :167 (proficiency), and the
            -- detail pane's identical pair at :356/:376. The ref sets the normal-skill pair BEFORE
            -- its `skillMaxRank` gate and lets the proficiency arm overwrite it; setting each arm's
            -- own pair here is the same result with no dead write. The ref's THIRD writer of this
            -- texture — the `skillCostType == 1/2/3` green/yellow/red block at :96-111, and the
            -- `stepCost` "Learn <skill>" gray at :126 — is unreachable for us and would be
            -- overwritten here even if it weren't: `stepCost`/`rankCost` are always nil and
            -- `numTempPoints` always 0 (skills.rs's module doc — dead 1.12 data, deviation 1/5), so
            -- every entry row takes the ref's own `else -- Normal skill` arm.
            local bgTexture = getglobal(bar:GetName() .. "Background")
            nameText:SetText(skillName)
            nameText:SetTextColor(NORMAL_FONT_COLOR.r, NORMAL_FONT_COLOR.g, NORMAL_FONT_COLOR.b)
            rankText:SetTextColor(HIGHLIGHT_FONT_COLOR.r, HIGHLIGHT_FONT_COLOR.g, HIGHLIGHT_FONT_COLOR.b)
            if skillMaxRank == 1 then
                -- ref SkillFrame.lua:161-167 verbatim: "If max rank in a skill is 1 assume that
                -- its a proficiency" — a FULL gray bar and NO rank text. Two kinds of line land
                -- here, and the ref can't tell them apart because it doesn't need to: the armor
                -- proficiencies, which the server really does report as 1/1, and the single-rank
                -- lines (class skills, Dual Wield, racials, the per-mount riding lines) whose
                -- `skillMaxRank` the engine already overrode to 1 off
                -- `SkillRaceClassInfo.flags & 0x400` (skills.rs's `SkillEntry::mono`) — which is
                -- why a hunter's `Beast Mastery 300/300` draws gray and numberless here, exactly
                -- as it does in the real client.
                bar:SetMinMaxValues(0, 1)
                bar:SetValue(1)
                bar:SetStatusBarColor(0.5, 0.5, 0.5)
                rankText:SetText("")
                bgTexture:SetVertexColor(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.5)
            elseif skillMaxRank == 0 then
                -- Not reachable off a live server (a line the player HAS always carries a max ≥ 1)
                -- and the ref leaves this case to fall through its own if/elseif untouched —
                -- which, on a recycled row, would leave the PREVIOUS skill's bar and rank text
                -- sitting there. We blank instead: a stale-state hole is a quirk, not behaviour.
                bar:SetMinMaxValues(0, 1)
                bar:SetValue(0)
                bar:SetStatusBarColor(0, 0, 0, 0)
                rankText:SetText("")
                -- back to the template's own declared base, so a recycled row shows a neutral empty
                -- trough rather than the previous skill's blue or white. The base lives in the
                -- TEXEL (the template's `<Color 1,1,1,0.2>`), so restoring it means an IDENTITY
                -- vertex colour — writing 0.2 here would multiply it to 0.04 (decision 1101).
                bgTexture:SetVertexColor(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0)
            else
                bar:SetStatusBarColor(0.0, 0.0, 1.0, 0.5)
                bgTexture:SetVertexColor(0.0, 0.0, 0.75, 0.5)
                bar:SetMinMaxValues(0, skillMaxRank)
                bar:SetValue(skillRank)
                -- the ref's rank-text law (SkillFrame.lua:178-186), re-expressed here (this file's
                -- header comment, deviation 4).
                if skillModifier == 0 then
                    rankText:SetText(skillRank .. "/" .. skillMaxRank)
                else
                    local color = RED_FONT_COLOR_CODE
                    if skillModifier > 0 then
                        color = GREEN_FONT_COLOR_CODE .. "+"
                    end
                    rankText:SetText(skillRank .. " (" .. color .. skillModifier .. FONT_COLOR_CODE_CLOSE .. ")/" .. skillMaxRank)
                end
            end
        end

        -- Fill the detail pane (deviation 1) for the current `GetSelectedSkill()`, or blank it
        -- when nothing is selected / the selection isn't a visible entry. The description body is
        -- the ref's own (ref SkillFrame.lua l.211-217 hide/show alongside the bar; l.262 the
        -- SKILL_DESCRIPTION format): `skillType` stays "" in EVERY reachable 1.12 branch — the
        -- ref's single assignment ("Tertiary Skill:") is commented out in the reference itself —
        -- so the format's first slot renders empty, byte-faithful. The unlearn button rides the
        -- same fill (ref l.220-226): shown only for an abandonable line, carrying the name the
        -- confirm popup formats and the index its accept abandons.
        function BenillaSkillFrame_UpdateDetail()
            local bar = getglobal("SkillDetailBar")
            local desc = getglobal("SkillDetailDescriptionText")
            local unlearn = getglobal("SkillDetailUnlearnButton")
            local index = GetSelectedSkill()
            if index == 0 then
                bar:Hide()
                desc:Hide()
                unlearn:Hide()
                return
            end
            local skillName, isHeader, _, skillRank, _, skillModifier, skillMaxRank, isAbandonable = GetSkillLineInfo(index)
            if not skillName or isHeader then
                bar:Hide()
                desc:Hide()
                unlearn:Hide()
                return
            end
            bar:Show()
            BenillaSkillFrame_PaintBar(bar, skillName, skillRank, skillModifier, skillMaxRank)
            if isAbandonable then
                unlearn.skillName = skillName
                unlearn.index = index
                unlearn:Show()
            else
                unlearn:Hide()
            end
            local skillType = ""
            local skillDescription = select(13, GetSkillLineInfo(index)) or ""
            desc:SetText(format(SKILL_DESCRIPTION, skillType, skillDescription))
            desc:Show()
        end

        -- ── The abandon confirm + the unlearn button's handlers ──────────────────────────────────
        -- The dialog is ref StaticPopup.lua:1121-1133 verbatim (minus the vestigial TEXT()
        -- wrapper); its OnAccept receives dialog.data — the visible index the button stashed.
        -- CANCEL stays the bare GlobalStrings global (DeathFrame.xml's own convention — the app
        -- loads the real GlobalStrings.lua before any window file). The handlers are chunk
        -- functions, NOT inline bodies, so the chunk-local strings above are visible to them
        -- (the nil-"All" chunk-boundary rule, TradeSkillFrame.xml's deviation notes).
        StaticPopupDialogs["UNLEARN_SKILL"] = {
            text = UNLEARN_SKILL,
            button1 = UNLEARN,
            button2 = CANCEL,
            OnAccept = function(index)
                AbandonSkill(index)
            end,
            timeout = 60,
            exclusive = 1,
            whileDead = 1,
            showAlert = 1,
            hideOnEscape = 1
        }

        function BenillaSkillUnlearnButton_OnClick(btn)
            local dialog = StaticPopup_Show("UNLEARN_SKILL", btn.skillName)
            if dialog then
                dialog.data = btn.index
            end
        end

        function BenillaSkillUnlearnButton_OnEnter(btn)
            GameTooltip:SetOwner(btn, "ANCHOR_RIGHT")
            GameTooltip:SetText(UNLEARN_SKILL_TOOLTIP)
        end

        -- Paint list slot `i` (1..12) from the visible row at `index` (ref SkillFrame_SetStatusBar,
        -- l.24-188 — the header branch, l.55-69, and the entry branch, l.76-187, collapsed: the
        -- skillCostType coloring + stepCost/rankCost training-up arrows never apply here, since
        -- GetSkillLineInfo always reports them nil/0, this file's header comment deviation 1).
        function BenillaSkillFrame_SetRow(i, index, numRows)
            local bar = getglobal("SkillRankFrame" .. i)
            local label = getglobal("SkillTypeLabel" .. i)

            if index > numRows then
                bar:Hide()
                bar.skillIndex = nil
                label:Hide()
                label.skillIndex = nil
                return
            end

            local skillName, isHeader, isExpanded, skillRank, _, skillModifier, skillMaxRank = GetSkillLineInfo(index)

            if isHeader then
                bar:Hide()
                bar.skillIndex = nil
                label:Show()
                label.skillIndex = index
                label:SetText(skillName)
                if isExpanded then
                    label:SetNormalTexture("Interface\\Buttons\\UI-MinusButton-Up")
                else
                    label:SetNormalTexture("Interface\\Buttons\\UI-PlusButton-Up")
                end
                return
            end

            label:Hide()
            label.skillIndex = nil
            bar:Show()
            bar.skillIndex = index
            BenillaSkillFrame_PaintBar(bar, skillName, skillRank, skillModifier, skillMaxRank)
        end

        -- The list page (ref SkillFrame_UpdateSkills, l.402-448 — the dead
        -- `UnitCharacterPoints("player")`/`SkillFrame.UpdatedSkillPoints` read, l.437-440, whose
        -- result nothing downstream ever consumes even in the ref itself, is dropped — the
        -- TradeSkillFrame.xml "ref's own dead code is dropped" precedent).
        function BenillaSkillFrame_Update()
            local numRows = GetNumSkillLines()
            local scrollFrame = getglobal("SkillListScrollFrame")
            FauxScrollFrame_Update(scrollFrame, numRows, SKILLFRAME_SKILLS_DISPLAYED, SKILLFRAME_SKILL_HEIGHT)
            local offset = FauxScrollFrame_GetOffset(scrollFrame)

            local highlight = getglobal("SkillHighlight")
            highlight:Hide()
            local selected = GetSelectedSkill()

            for i = 1, SKILLFRAME_SKILLS_DISPLAYED do
                local index = i + offset
                BenillaSkillFrame_SetRow(i, index, numRows)
                if selected == index and index <= numRows then
                    highlight:SetPoint("TOPLEFT", getglobal("SkillRankFrame" .. i), "TOPLEFT", -5, 0)
                    highlight:Show()
                end
            end

            -- The collapse-all tab's +/- icon (ref l.417-429's own numHeaders/notExpanded scan).
            local allExpanded = true
            for i = 1, numRows do
                local _, isHeader, isExpanded = GetSkillLineInfo(i)
                if isHeader and not isExpanded then
                    allExpanded = false
                end
            end
            local collapseAll = getglobal("SkillCollapseAllButton")
            if numRows == 0 then
                collapseAll:Disable()
            else
                collapseAll:Enable()
            end
            if allExpanded then
                collapseAll.collapsed = nil
                collapseAll:SetNormalTexture("Interface\\Buttons\\UI-MinusButton-Up")
            else
                collapseAll.collapsed = 1
                collapseAll:SetNormalTexture("Interface\\Buttons\\UI-PlusButton-Up")
            end

            BenillaSkillFrame_UpdateDetail()
        end

        -- A rank-bar click selects it (ref SkillBar_OnClick, l.450-455).
        function BenillaSkillRankFrame_OnClick(bar)
            local index = bar.skillIndex
            if not index then
                return
            end
            SetSelectedSkill(index)
            BenillaSkillFrame_Update()
        end

        -- A header click folds/unfolds its group (ref SkillLabelTemplate's own OnClick, l.72-80).
        function BenillaSkillTypeLabel_OnClick(label)
            local index = label.skillIndex
            if not index then
                return
            end
            local _, _, isExpanded = GetSkillLineInfo(index)
            if isExpanded then
                CollapseSkillHeader(index)
                -- A fold reshuffles visible indices — an UNLEARN_SKILL confirm armed for a row
                -- that no longer holds the selection must not fire against the wrong line (ref
                -- SkillLabelTemplate's own OnClick, ref SkillFrame.xml l.72-78).
                local dialog = StaticPopup_FindVisible("UNLEARN_SKILL")
                if dialog and dialog.data ~= GetSelectedSkill() then
                    StaticPopup_Hide("UNLEARN_SKILL")
                end
            else
                ExpandSkillHeader(index)
            end
            BenillaSkillFrame_Update()
        end

        -- The collapse-all tab (ref SkillFrameCollapseAllButton's own isExpanded flag, l.303-309,
        -- driven the TrainerFrame.xml BenillaTrainerCollapseAllButton way since this engine's
        -- CollapseSkillHeader(0)/ExpandSkillHeader(0) already fold/unfold every group at once).
        function BenillaSkillCollapseAllButton_OnClick()
            local b = getglobal("SkillCollapseAllButton")
            if b.collapsed then
                ExpandSkillHeader(0)
            else
                CollapseSkillHeader(0)
                FauxScrollFrame_SetOffset(getglobal("SkillListScrollFrame"), 0)
            end
            BenillaSkillFrame_Update()
        end

        -- The window's wheel handler (bubbled up the parent chain from a row) → one row via the faux
        -- kit (TrainerFrame.xml's own note: the engine bubbles a spin up the parent chain).
        function BenillaSkillFrame_OnMouseWheel(delta)
            BenillaFauxScrollFrame_OnMouseWheel(getglobal("SkillListScrollFrame"), delta)
        end

        -- ── Lifecycle (ref SkillFrame_OnLoad/_OnShow/_OnEvent, l.4-22, collapsed to the events this
        -- page's feed actually fires: CHARACTER_POINTS_CHANGED backs the training-point economy this
        -- pane doesn't ship, this file's header comment deviation 1). ─────────────────────────────────
        function SkillFrame_OnLoad()
            local frame = this
            frame:RegisterEvent("SKILL_LINES_CHANGED")
            getglobal("SkillListScrollFrame").updateFunc = BenillaSkillFrame_Update
            -- The description body hangs under the detail bar — anchored here, not in XML,
            -- because the bar is a child frame declared after the page's layers and anchors
            -- resolve at SetPoint time (an XML forward reference silently lands on the page;
            -- the MailFrame error-text OnLoad precedent, ref MailFrame.xml l.1040). Cleared
            -- first: the load-time implicit anchor (decision 1310) seated this justifyH="LEFT"
            -- string at the page's LEFT, and SetPoint replaces only its own point -- without the
            -- clear both anchors stand and the left/center edges resolve off the page, not the
            -- bar. (The ref needs no clear on ITS file only because its XML anchors the string.)
            SkillDetailDescriptionText:ClearAllPoints()
            SkillDetailDescriptionText:SetPoint("TOPLEFT", "SkillDetailBar", "BOTTOMLEFT", -2, -10)
        end

        function SkillFrame_OnShow()
            BenillaSkillFrame_Update()
        end

        function SkillFrame_OnEvent(event)
            local frame = this
            if event == "SKILL_LINES_CHANGED" and frame:IsVisible() then
                BenillaSkillFrame_Update()
            end
        end
    ]]></Script>

    <!--
        The rank StatusBar row (ref SkillStatusBarTemplate, l.4-65 — the FillBar dropped, this file's
        header comment deviation 5): 271×15, name+rank overlaid, the Border child Button for OnClick
        + hover highlight (TradeSkillFrame.xml's own BenillaTradeSkillRankFrame shape, verbatim).
    -->
    <StatusBar name="BenillaSkillRankTemplate" virtual="true" hidden="true" drawLayer="BACKGROUND" minValue="0" maxValue="1" defaultValue="0">
        <Size><AbsDimension x="271" y="15"/></Size>
        <Layers>
            <Layer level="ARTWORK">
                <FontString name="$parentSkillName" inherits="GameFontNormalSmall">
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="LEFT" relativePoint="LEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="6" y="1"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </FontString>
                <FontString name="$parentSkillRank" inherits="GameFontHighlightSmall" justifyH="LEFT">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="128" y="0"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="LEFT" relativeTo="$parentSkillName" relativePoint="RIGHT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="13" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </FontString>
            </Layer>
            <Layer level="BACKGROUND">
                <Texture name="$parentBackground"><Color r="1.0" g="1.0" b="1.0" a="0.2"/></Texture>
            </Layer>
        </Layers>
        <Frames>
            <Button name="$parentBorder">
                <Size><AbsDimension x="281" y="32"/></Size>
                <Anchors><Anchor point="LEFT" relativePoint="LEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="-5" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                <NormalTexture file="Interface\PaperDollInfoFrame\UI-Character-Skills-BarBorder"/>
                <HighlightTexture file="Interface\PaperDollInfoFrame\UI-Character-Skills-BarBorderHighlight"/>
                <Scripts><OnClick>BenillaSkillRankFrame_OnClick(self:GetParent())</OnClick></Scripts>
            </Button>
        </Frames>
        <BarTexture name="$parentBar" file="Interface\PaperDollInfoFrame\UI-Character-Skills-Bar"/>
        <BarColor r="0.25" g="0.25" b="0.75"/>
    </StatusBar>

    <!--
        The category header row (ref SkillLabelTemplate, l.66-129, minus the DisabledTexture — this
        window never Disable()s a header): 285×14, the +/- fold icon + name text.
    -->
    <Button name="BenillaSkillHeaderTemplate" virtual="true" hidden="true">
        <Size><AbsDimension x="285" y="14"/></Size>
        <Scripts><OnClick>BenillaSkillTypeLabel_OnClick(self)</OnClick></Scripts>
        <NormalTexture file="Interface\Buttons\UI-MinusButton-UP">
            <Size><AbsDimension x="16" y="16"/></Size>
            <Anchors><Anchor point="LEFT" relativePoint="LEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="3" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
        </NormalTexture>
        <HighlightTexture file="Interface\Buttons\UI-PlusButton-Hilight" alphaMode="ADD">
            <Size><AbsDimension x="16" y="16"/></Size>
            <Anchors><Anchor point="LEFT" relativePoint="LEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="3" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
        </HighlightTexture>
        <ButtonText>
            <Anchors><Anchor point="LEFT" relativePoint="LEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="25" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
        </ButtonText>
        <NormalFont inherits="GameFontHighlight" justifyH="LEFT"/>
    </Button>

    <!-- id=4, the ref's own: a page's id is the slot it occupies in the WINDOW'S OWN tab row, and
         ToggleCharacter selects the tab from it (ref CharacterFrame.lua:11). This was 3 while
         Reputation (the ref's 3) was not built; ReputationFrame.xml landed and took that slot, so
         Skills is back on the reference's number. `character_tests.rs` pins every page's id against
         its slot in BENILLA_CHARACTERFRAME_SUBFRAMES, which is what made the renumber loud rather
         than silent — exactly as this comment predicted. -->
    <Frame name="SkillFrame" enableMouse="true" parent="CharacterFrame" hidden="true" id="4">
        <!-- The real 384×512 page. No <Anchors relativeTo> substitute for true parenting exists
             (this file's header comment) — pinned to CharacterFrame's own TOPLEFT by name. -->
        <Size><AbsDimension x="384" y="512"/></Size>
        <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativeTo="CharacterFrame" relativePoint="TOPLEFT"/></Anchors>
        <!-- Transcribed for fidelity (ref l.131-133); no loader wiring exists yet for the hit-rect
             shrink (TradeSkillFrame.xml's own "transcribe the hook even if nothing drives it yet"
             posture, TalentFrame.xml's precedent). -->
        <HitRectInsets><AbsInset left="0" right="30" top="0" bottom="75"/></HitRectInsets>
        <Layers>
            <!-- The shared quadrant background (ref l.136-183): NO portrait redraw here (this file's
                 header comment) — "General" TopLeft/TopRight (the same variant every PaperDollInfoFrame
                 page shares, carrying the portrait-ring cutout) + SkillFrame's own BotLeft/BotRight. -->
            <Layer level="BACKGROUND">
                <Texture file="Interface\PaperDollInfoFrame\UI-Character-General-TopLeft">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="256" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativePoint="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="2" y="-1"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <Texture file="Interface\PaperDollInfoFrame\UI-Character-General-TopRight">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="128" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPRIGHT" relativePoint="TOPRIGHT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="2" y="-1"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <Texture file="Interface\PaperDollInfoFrame\SkillFrame-BotLeft">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="256" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="BOTTOMLEFT" relativePoint="BOTTOMLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="2" y="-1"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <Texture file="Interface\PaperDollInfoFrame\SkillFrame-BotRight">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="128" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="BOTTOMRIGHT" relativePoint="BOTTOMRIGHT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="2" y="-1"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </Texture>
            </Layer>
            <!-- The divider bar below the list, above the detail pane (ref l.186-211's own
                 TOPLEFT(15,-290); nudged to -305 here to clear this file's own 12-row chain, whose
                 last row sits slightly lower than the ref's fixed-slot geometry — a pixel-fit
                 adjustment, not a structural deviation). -->
            <Layer level="ARTWORK">
                <Texture name="SkillHorizontalBarLeft" file="Interface\ClassTrainerFrame\UI-ClassTrainer-HorizontalBar">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="256" y="16"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativePoint="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="15" y="-305"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                    <TexCoords left="0" right="1.0" top="0" bottom="0.25"/>
